The capital reinvestment fund finances terminal expansions, runway resurfacing cycles, equipment replacement, and new facilities across the airport network. The route development fund provides incentives for airlines to establish new routes to and from Balboan airports, including fee waivers during launch periods, marketing support, and guaranteed minimum revenue for qualifying routes. The remittance to the national treasury flows to the general fund as agency revenue, contributing to national expenditure on non-aviation programmes.

