Airports are designated as international or domestic by the Ministry of Transport on the recommendation of the authority. International airports are those with customs, immigration, and quarantine facilities capable of handling international flights, while domestic airports serve only domestic traffic. The authority is responsible for maintaining essential services to remote and low-traffic airports that would not be commercially viable on their own, funded through the cross-subsidy model rather than direct government appropriations.

== ICAO naming convention ==

Balboan airport ICAO codes follow the convention of the IATA code followed by the suffix "IB" (for Istme de Balboa). For example, Sant Cristòfor International Airport has IATA code SCI and ICAO code SCIB. The sole exception is the [[International City of Areza]], which is not part of Balboa and whose former airport ([[Areza International Airport]]) used the ICAO prefix AEIB.

